WEBVTT

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.990
That's it, Narumi!

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.330
That's why I scouted you.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.710
When hit with spiritual force,

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.840
their fluids oscillate
to the point of explosion.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.710
Let me do the rest, Guy.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.980
Before dawn, when the stars paint the sky

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.900
I am searching for the thing I lost

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.650
With a restless heart
Under the sun yet in the dark

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.280
I patch together little prayers
to light my path

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.040
I don't need anything,
as my hands are full

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.880
My hands are full of emptiness

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.670
Please, just once, nod for me

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.640
Just once, reach out to me like the mirror

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.270
I will live for that single moment,
that single second

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.770
All the rest can just burn away

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.780
What's right for me is for me alone

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:24.910
Whatever the path, I'll follow it to you

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:29.410
This feeling grows and grows,
deep inside my heart

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.960
For one single reason

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:41.010
I continue to climb up on the stage

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.720
#7 Demonic

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.560
You're pretty good.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.230
You must be the
new shirogane.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.440
Call me whatever you want,
before I take away that voice of yours.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.460
Why?

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.800
Why am I fighting?

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.420
Why am I here?

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.800
There's only one answer.
To protect the children.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.180
I was given that Aqua Vitae thing.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.810
That means I'm living off the kids' lives.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.690
In which case,
I have to fight for them.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.280
Go, Anselmus.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:55.120
Nice dodge.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.210
But I still got you pretty deep.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.630
It's your turn now.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.800
Go, Paulmann!

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.970
Narumi, turn the switch on your shoulder.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.350
Impossible...

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:19.690
My blade stopped by a measly human?

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.820
Hear that?

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.690
It's the sound of my wounds healing

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.490
thanks to that infernal Aqua Vitae.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.330
I'm no longer a human.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.080
I'm the demon that will crush you.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.630
Is that so?

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.340
Narumi!

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.670
Farewell, shirogane!

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.810
Is that possible...?

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:56.890
It sure is.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:02.270
Anselmus!

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.860
I have no choice.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.650
What? My spikes are stuck.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.860
Where are you going?

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.370
Take me with you.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.530
He's flexing his muscles.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.950
You're mad. Don't you feel any pain?

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:24.840
You machines will never understand.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.630
Those kids' bright futures
were snatched away

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:33.300
and replaced with nothing but despair.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:36.720
I couldn't do anything for them here.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:41.390
I just stood by and watched helplessly.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:45.270
So now...

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:51.700
the least I can do is to feel
a fraction of their pain.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.620
Or else I won't even know why I exist.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:14.930
It's safe now.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.890
I beat them all up.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.360
Damn it.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:32.360
I scared them.

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:35.740
I...

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.450
I...

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.250
I'm sorry, kids.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.710
You can't blame them.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.460
Fighting like that
in front of the children.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.380
Guy.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.970
About you wanting to scout me,

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:57.390
I accept.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:58.720
Thanks.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.480
Lucille, can I borrow that thing?

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.810
You want to wear it?

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.310
Yeah.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:11.610
I can't scare the kids
anymore than I already have.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:14.990
Dr. Banhart.

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:21.330
Just as you wear yourselves out
caring for ZONAPHA patients,

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.500
I won't stop fighting the automata.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.340
Even if the children hate me,
even if you despise me.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.050
So please.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:36.010
Find a cure for ZONAPHA syndrome
as fast as you can.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.470
Narumi!

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.730
Tom.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.690
Thank you, Narumi.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.230
Thank you.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.740
Anything for them.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.530
If I have to become a fighting demon,
so be it.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:04.410
To protect the kids,

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:08.000
I will become a shirogane.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.520
Narumi, it's me, Masaru.

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:30.730
Shirogane and I joined
the Nakamachi Circus.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.520
We're off on a trip for summer vacation.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.900
But we don't have enough money
to put on a show.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.370
Gotta save up to open the circus.
Get to it!

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:43.490
Yes, sir!

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.490
"IZU BANANA ZOO"

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.710
We rode on Sis's ride,
so now it's my turn.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.770
Dear me.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:11.810
I love watching entertainers
do their thing.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.060
I just can't leave them alone.

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.860
You're pretty good, Whiteface.

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:26.580
This is out of the blue,
but why don't we make a bet?

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:30.710
Let's play a game for some money.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.710
Sure. I'm in.

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:40.470
The first one to hit the other's body
with our gear wins.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:41.930
Okay.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.730
What are you doing? Let's begin.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:51.940
What are you doing?

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.650
The game's already begun.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.190
He still has his back to me.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.740
You'll regret it!

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:04.990
I guess I lost.

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:08.830
You nicked my hair. You're good.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.620
A girl?

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.830
Mine didn't reach you.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.170
What circus are you from?

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:21.170
You called me "Whiteface"
rather than "clown."

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.890
Most people wouldn't know
the types of clowns.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.180
I see.

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:30.850
You're quite a girl.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.810
You make me forget about my job.
I like you.

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:41.740
You made money
by performing on your own?

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:45.820
I want to make money like that
instead of construction work.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.120
You don't have Shirogane's
good looks or great tricks.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:54.960
This is the money I've made
as a member of Nakamachi Circus.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:56.540
Here.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:10:00.090
I suppose I can't refuse.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:01.380
Good job.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.880
Hands off.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:07.930
Did anything fun happen today, Shirogane?

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:11.970
Yes, actually, I became friends
with a strange person.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:15.100
"STRAWBERRY MILK"

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:17.980
I was born into an American circus family.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:24.240
I had always thought I'd become
a knife thrower like my dad.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:27.740
But I didn't.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.990
Did something happen?

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.040
Ever heard of ZONAPHA syndrome?

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.910
Ugh, of course not.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:39.000
It's this strange disease,
and my kid brother got it.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:44.920
Treatments cost money, right?
My parents worked to death.

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:47.130
I wanted to make money too,

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:51.260
but I wasn't good with the knife
like my dad was.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:52.770
And your brother?

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.230
He died at age 15.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.270
What's wrong?

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:06.780
I knew a man who had ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.950
Really? What happened to him?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.290
I see.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.540
What a coincidence.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:20.290
I feel like we could be good friends.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:23.630
My name's Vilma. You?

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:26.630
Shirogane.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:33.140
Wow, that's rare of you
to talk to someone like that.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:35.060
I'm surprised, too.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.850
Before, I only cared about
whether people were my enemy.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:43.820
If they weren't, that was it.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.530
Meaningless conversations
were a pain for me.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:54.990
But since I met you, talking to people
hasn't been that bad.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:11:59.790
Do you think I'm losing it?

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:04.710
I like you better like this.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.090
Thank you.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:09.930
Oh?

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:14.180
I forgot to return the balloons
to the zoo.

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:16.850
I'll be right back.

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:18.850
Later.

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:23.860
This is the last one.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.070
Forgive me, Jim.

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:34.070
I'm so glad Shirogane said that.

00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:37.330
Maybe she's been able to forget
about Narumi.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.080
-I'm back.
-Oh, hi.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.130
Where's Mr. Masaru?

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:49.300
I thought he went to get you.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.970
Sorry, kid.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.180
But I have to kill you.

00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:04.900
You must think that's unfair,
but some people just don't get to live.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:10.780
I knew this would happen someday.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:13.360
So I'd made up my mind

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:18.410
not to cry when the time came.

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:20.910
Mr. Masaru!

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:24.420
You!

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:30.920
Arlequin!

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.090
What?

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:36.140
A puppet?

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:37.970
Are you okay?

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.010
Yeah.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.180
Vilma. It's you, isn't it?

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:44.020
I'm surprised too

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:48.110
that the clown from earlier
is my target's bodyguard.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.530
And a puppeteer, no less.

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:52.030
Target?

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:57.530
So you're an assassin.
Did Mr. Masaru's brothers hire you?

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:00.120
Strictly business. I can't say.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:03.620
Is this the person you made friends with
at the zoo?

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.830
-But she...
-Stand back.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:10.920
Too bad. I thought we could be friends.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:16.050
Funny, though.
He doesn't have anybody backing him up.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:19.260
So who's paying you?

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:22.020
It's not for free, is it?

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:24.940
Shirogane!

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:29.310
Black Vilma's Shooting Stars
are faster than a bullet.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.240
You can still move?

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:36.070
-Shirogane, no!
-I'm fine.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:41.080
As long as you're in danger,
my knees shall not touch the ground.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.830
Your showtime is over.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.830
Time for you to sleep!

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:48.670
Shi...

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:54.380
Nobody shall lay
a single finger on Mr. Masaru.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.970
You... You can't be human.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.600
-If you're going to kill, kill me!
-Mr. Masaru!

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:05.430
At first I thought you didn't
really mean to kill me.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:08.850
You're such a good knife thrower,
but you missed me twice.

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:12.400
It was to scare you stiff
to keep you from escaping.

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.490
You wouldn't do that
if you were going to kill me.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:18.910
That's why I thought
you were actually a good person.

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:23.040
But you are a bad person after all.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.920
Don't look at me like that.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:33.000
Jim!

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:41.220
Why aren't you dead yet?

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.060
You asked who was paying me.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:46.980
I'll tell you.

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.020
I need no pay.

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:51.900
As long as I can protect him.

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:56.570
As long as he's safe,
my body will not even hope for a tomorrow.

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:04.030
-Shirogane, don't die! An ambulance...
-Look.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:09.250
Your wounds. Why?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:13.590
I have a special life within me.

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.880
Well, what do you know.

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:19.930
A monster is protecting my target.

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:23.470
But I can't back down, either.

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:24.890
Arlequin!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.810
Don't, you'll die!

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:33.270
I don't mind.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:36.280
If it's to protect you,
my life is nothing.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:40.280
No! I want you to live.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:43.910
You said you'd protect me
and become human again.

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.040
So you can't die until you do.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.540
Live!

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:52.960
What are they talking about?

00:16:53.420 --> 00:16:56.630
He's saying the same thing as Jim.

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:01.090
Jim is in pain.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.430
We pay you good money
but you do nothing to save him!

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:05.970
Vilma.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:09.430
Remember what Dad said?

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.350
Entertainers shouldn't show anger.

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:16.480
Not in front of the audience.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:21.150
So do your trick.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.740
Let's entertain them.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.160
No...

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:31.330
When I get better...

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:35.170
you said we'd do a show together.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:41.670
Jim and Vilma's "Wild West Knife Show."

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.180
I want to see it too,

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:47.600
before I go.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:52.020
Don't worry.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:56.230
Black Vilma's Shooting Stars...

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:59.020
they're faster than a bullet.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.330
Jim!

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:17.130
You can't die, Vilma.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:19.880
Live on...

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.680
This is the last one, I promise.

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:43.400
Sorry, Jim.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:47.740
I missed again.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:04.130
If you try anything funny, you die.

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.680
Mr. Masaru wished
for you to be brought here.

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:12.430
-Is this your circus?
-That's right.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:17.440
We told them we found you unconscious
and had them take you in.

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:22.980
What a joke.

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.900
I tried to kill you.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:26.400
Quiet.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:31.910
An 11 year-old boy saved you,
who came to kill him.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.330
You know, I'm a professional.

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:40.420
I understand. That's why I'm here.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:42.790
You are my target.

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:48.800
If you want to stay alive,
leave now and never return.

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:53.050
Is he that important to you?

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:56.730
He is my everything.

00:19:57.180 --> 00:19:58.770
You monster.

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:00.480
But you know what?

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:04.440
A monster's teary face must be sexy.

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:06.690
Ooh, scary.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:13.410
You must've tried to kill me
when I became unconscious.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.290
Yes, but...

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.330
Don't, you're not a killer.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.080
Even if it is for me.

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:23.840
But this woman...

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:29.590
How could you understand how precious
life is if you don't care for your own?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:33.010
You're right.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:36.470
What are you doing?

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:39.850
-I can't just leave her here.
-But...

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:43.360
What if she tries to kill you again?

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:44.860
Sorry.

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.940
But I'll become stronger, too.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:52.610
Then will you do one thing?

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.290
Will you drink my blood?

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:58.290
Your blood?

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:02.790
It will protect you from injuries
and diseases.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:05.880
Would you rather not?

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:11.170
I'll drink it
if that'll make you feel easier.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:16.890
People often told me that I was like
a cold puppet, warding people off.

00:21:17.680 --> 00:21:22.730
But I met Mr. Masaru and other people
and learned much.

00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:25.690
And now, I've come to think

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.400
that I want to change.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:37.580
I've come up with an idea.
Something more fun than killing people.

00:21:38.950 --> 00:21:42.830
So honey, will you ask them for me?

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:46.920
You want to join our circus?

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:50.880
We might be a tiny circus,
but we won't let just anybody...

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:57.510
Ladies and gentlemen. I'm a knife thrower.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:21:59.430
She's one of us!

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:04.690
And so, we gained another member.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:09.860
Narumi, the circus sure is great, huh?

00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:16.820
Fly up high, Marionette

00:22:16.990 --> 00:22:19.160
Turn to ash, gracefully

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:23.660
My only purpose in life was to fight

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:28.460
Why am I so angry
even I dump my humanity

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:34.840
Without you, I can't smile anymore

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:39.970
I assume that I am to be blamed

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:44.480
Like a puppet that can't smile naturally

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:49.690
I feel like someone is pulling my strings

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:53.440
What am I even living for?

00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:57.700
I was hurt, and thought
that nobody would understand

00:22:57.860 --> 00:23:02.830
But you came along,
and took me in your arms

00:23:02.990 --> 00:23:09.040
I felt my tangled arms and legs

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:11.420
become free

00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:14.050
Fly up high, Marionette

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:16.380
I think now I can reach you

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:20.890
Before I met you, I was empty

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:25.680
Now I have something
I'd give my all to protect

00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:32.070
You taught me how to feel,
the feeling of sorrow too
